        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.22371/2610.22371v1/pipeline_v2_2.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of Gen4P.The input video is encoded into scene tokens𝐅\\mathbf{F}in a single passby theVideo Generative Encoder, which consists of a frozen VAE encoder and DiT, an optional frozen Depth-LoRA, and a trainable 4D-LoRA.\nThe cross-attentionQuery Decoderis queried independently for each query𝐪⁡(u,v,tsrc,ttgt,tcam)\\mathbf{q}(u,v,t_{\\mathrm{src}},t_{\\mathrm{tgt}},t_{\\mathrm{cam}}), where\nthe query timestamps are parameterized as continuous time embeddings.\nThe decoder outputs the corresponding 3D and 2D point attributes, enabling the full construction of 3D tracks, depth maps and camera poses.",
                "position": 375
            }
        ]
